WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.327
Question twelve.

00:00:01.327 --> 00:00:08.130
Step one: macro scan. It asks the place value of the third one-bit from the right.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.365
One mark. Command words: “place value”.

00:00:11.365 --> 00:00:12.858
Step two: denoise.

00:00:12.858 --> 00:00:16.591
Useful, in yellow: one zero one one zero one.

00:00:16.591 --> 00:00:22.066
In cyan: “from right to left” and “third bit with face value one”.

00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:27.707
Useless red herring: the whole number’s decimal value — kick it out.

00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:29.201
Step three: draft.

00:00:29.201 --> 00:00:33.100
From the right: two to the zero is one — first.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.911
Two to the one is zero, skip; two squared is one — second.

00:00:37.911 --> 00:00:39.985
Two cubed is one — third.

00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:41.395
Step four: P O E.

00:00:41.395 --> 00:00:44.879
A, two to the one: that bit is zero — cut.

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:48.032
B, two squared: only the second — cut.

00:00:48.032 --> 00:00:51.599
D, two to the four: that bit is zero — cut.

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:58.816
Step five: sanity check and lock. Counting to the third one lands exactly on two cubed.

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:01.056
So the correct answer is C.
